\section{Assumptions}
\label{sec:assumptions}
In our analysis we rely on the following weak assumptions on the functions $f_i.$ 
\begin{assumption}
  \label{ass:lower_bound}
  There exists $f^* \in \R$ such that $f(x) \geq f^*$ for all $x \in \R^d$.
\end{assumption}
\begin{assumption}
  \label{ass:lipschitz_constant}
  There exists $L_{-}\geq 0$ such that $\norm{\nabla f(x) - \nabla f(y)} \leq L_{-} \norm{x - y}$ for all $x, y \in \R^d.$
\end{assumption}
\begin{assumption}
  \label{ass:local_lipschitz_constant}
  For all $i \in [n],$ there existsa constant $L_{i}>0$ such that $\norm{\nabla f_i(x) - \nabla f_i(y)} \leq L_{i} \norm{x - y}$ for all $x, y \in \R^d.$
\end{assumption}

